README.md

```markdown
# Neural Search Engine

Production-ready web-scale neural search system combining Cerebras LLM inference with GPU-accelerated vector operations on Modal.

## Architecture

- **LLM Inference**: Cerebras (1400-1700 tok/s)
- **Vector Search**: Modal 8x B200 GPUs (1440GB VRAM, 64TB/s)
- **Cache**: Dragonfly Cloud (25x faster than Redis)
- **Metadata**: PostgreSQL + ScyllaDB
- **Telemetry**: KDB+ time-series database
- **Crawler**: 100+ concurrent workers (Inko)

## Languages

- Zig: API Gateway, streaming, HTTP/2
- Inko: Distributed crawler, actor concurrency
- Terra: Data preprocessing, LLVM optimization
- Futhark: GPU vector operations, HNSW search
- Bend: Parallel graph algorithms (PageRank, Louvain)
- Scopes: System orchestration
- Spiral: CUDA kernel generation
- Q/KDB+: Nanosecond telemetry

## Building

```bash
make build
```

## Deployment

```bash
make docker-up
make deploy
```

## Monitoring

```bash
make monitor
```
```

